{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Station closure effect, shared by server projector, Kotlin StationClosures, Swift StationClosures and web. A closure is active when status is not draft/cancelled and startsAt <= now < endsAt (endsAt null = until further notice). It applies to a (station, line) when the station is listed and lineIds is empty, the line is listed, or line is null. canBoard = every active closure is entry_only; canAlight = every active closure is exit_only. mode = most restrictive active mode by order closed > pass_through > exit_only > entry_only, except exit_only + entry_only together report closed. closureId = the active closure with the most restrictive mode (tie: smallest id). endsAt = null if any active closure is open-ended, else the latest end. When nothing is active, the earliest non-draft closure starting within the next 24 h (now < startsAt <= now+86400) is reported as upcoming. Departures are hidden from a station board when canBoard is false; planner may not board where canBoard is false or alight where canAlight is false; pass_through trains keep running through the station.",
